# What the deployed image needs is narrow: the `app` package (web app + the
# `app/cli` cron entrypoints), `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` for the release
# command, and the packaging metadata. Everything below is developer- or
# CI-facing and was shipping to production only because the Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .` against a five-line ignore file.
#
# Excluding a directory here makes it *absent at runtime*. A module under
# `app/` that reads from one of these paths therefore breaks the deployed
# container while CI, the deploy, and the digest verifier all stay green --
# the failure mode #688 was filed about. `scripts/check_runtime_entrypoints.py`
# reads this file and fails (E3) if anything under `app/` references an
# excluded path, so the two cannot drift apart. Add a directory here only
# after checking that guard passes.

fly.toml
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
__pycache__/
.envrc
.venv/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local tool output — present only on a developer machine, never needed at runtime.
.coverage
coverage.xml
.import_linter_cache

# Developer and CI trees — never executed inside the container.
scripts/
tests/
docs/
mockups/
deploy/
data/
node_modules/
